search/tags/","h":"#P","p":3},{"i":19,"t":"qa1 query-writing3","s":"Q","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/tags/","h":"#Q","p":3},{"i":21,"t":"scripting3","s":"S","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/tags/","h":"#S","p":3},{"i":23,"t":"text-annotation3","s":"T","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/tags/","h":"#T","p":3},{"i":50,"t":"Entity classification Classify funding organisations","s":"GRID+","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/classify-funders/","h":"","p":49},{"i":64,"t":"Entity classification Journal Geography Classifier","s":"Classify journal titles by geography","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/classify-journals/","h":"","p":63},{"i":66,"t":"Entity classification CRediT role assignment protocol","s":"Protocol for assigning CRediT roles","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/credit-taxonomy-protocol/","h":"","p":65},{"i":69,"t":"Input: Text descriptions of contributions written by individual researchers or team members. Output: One or more CRediT roles assigned to each researcher with justification based on the text.","s":"1.1. Define input and output","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/credit-taxonomy-protocol/","h":"#11-define-input-and-output","p":65},{"i":71,"t":"Text parsing interface (spreadsheet, NLP tool, or annotation platform) Reference document listing full CRediT taxonomy and definitions Version-controlled record of annotations for auditing","s":"1.2. Tools","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/credit-taxonomy-protocol/","h":"#12-tools","p":65},{"i":74,"t":"Convert text to lowercase Remove extraneous whitespace Correct spelling or OCR issues if applicable","s":"2.1. Standardize content","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/credit-taxonomy-protocol/","h":"#21-standardize-content","p":65},{"i":76,"t":"If descriptions include multiple clauses (e.g. “developed methods and collected data”), segment into atomic actions","s":"2.2. Segment compound entries","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/credit-taxonomy-protocol/","h":"#22-segment-compound-entries","p":65},{"i":78,"t":"Use a [rule-based classification] approach mapping key terms and phrases to CRediT roles. For ambiguous or multi-role expressions, assign all valid roles. CRediT Role Example Keywords/Phrases Conceptualization designed study, proposed idea, formulated hypothesis, defined aims, established research goals Data curation cleaned data, maintained database, added metadata, prepared data, organized dataset Formal analysis analyzed data, statistical analysis, modeled results, performed regression, applied algorithm Funding acquisition secured grant, applied for funding, wrote grant proposal, financial support Investigation conducted experiments, performed interviews, carried out fieldwork, data collection, ran tests Methodology developed method, designed protocol, created model, experiment design, algorithm design Project administration managed project, coordinated team, scheduled tasks, oversaw planning, managed workflow Resources provided samples, recruited patients, offered equipment, donated reagents, shared facilities Software wrote code, developed software, programmed, debugged, built scripts, designed software architecture Supervision supervised team, mentored researchers, oversaw research direction, guided team Validation verified results, replicated experiment, confirmed findings, cross-checked analysis, ran quality checks Visualization created figures, designed visualizations, plotted data, produced graphs, made charts Writing – original draft wrote manuscript, drafted paper, authored initial version, composed first draft Writing – review & editing reviewed draft, edited manuscript, revised text, provided feedback, commented on versions","s":"3. Role detection: mapping keywords and activities","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/credit-taxonomy-protocol/","h":"#3-role-detection-mapping-keywords-and-activities","p":65},{"i":81,"t":"For each activity clause, assign 1–3 CRediT roles based on keyword mapping and context If ambiguous between two roles (e.g., “wrote analysis pipeline”), allow dual assignment (e.g., Methodology + Software)","s":"4.1. Role matching","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/credit-taxonomy-protocol/","h":"#41-role-matching","p":65},{"i":83,"t":"If description is vague (e.g. “helped with project”), mark as Unclear and request clarification If multiple roles are potentially implied but not confirmed, use the most specific role available","s":"4.2. Ambiguity handling","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/credit-taxonomy-protocol/","h":"#42-ambiguity-handling","p":65},{"i":85,"t":"Record each assignment with: Original text Assigned role(s) Justification or matched keyword(s) Confidence level (High / Medium","s":"5. Documentation","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/entity/credit-taxonomy-protocol/","h":"#5-documentation","p":65},{"i":87,"t":"Bibliometric concept operationalisation Placeholder","s":"Placeholder","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/metrics/","h":"","p":86},{"i":89,"t":"Taxonomy and ontology support Placeholder","s":"Placeholder","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/ontology/","h":"","p":88},{"i":91,"t":"Prompt and instruction design Placeholder","s":"Placeholder","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/prompting/","h":"","p":90},{"i":93,"t":"Validation and QA Placeholder","s":"Placeholder","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/qa/","h":"","p":92},{"i":95,"t":"Search construction and refinement SmartSeeds--Boolean builder","s":"SmartSeeds: Boolean builder","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/search/boolean-builder/","h":"","p":94},{"i":97,"t":"Query writing and scripting DimQuery assistant","s":"DimQuery assistant","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/queries/dimquery-assistant/","h":"","p":96},{"i":99,"t":"Query writing and scripting DimDSL assistant","s":"DimDSL assistant","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/queries/dimdsl-assistant/","h":"","p":98},{"i":101,"t":"Text annotation and labeling Journal Geography Classifier","s":"Classify journal titles by geography","u":"/AIprotocolsforresearch/text/classify-journals/","h":"","p":100}],"index":{"version":"2.3.9